  "$comment": "Known search_path violations in the shipped migrations, tracked by issue 421.\nPR #420 does not edit shipped migrations; this file records each violation so the\nCI gate fails on NEW ones while these are fixed.\nEach entry is keyed on the routine's CATALOG IDENTITY: schema.name followed by the\nidentity arguments PostgreSQL reports, so renaming an argument or respelling a\nschema cannot silently re-point a waiver at a different routine.\nAn entry applies only while it is in date AND still matches a real violation. An\nentry with an invalid date, an expiry more than 180 days after `added`, an expiry\nbefore `added`, a missing issue, or a key that is not a catalog identity is REFUSED.\nAn expired entry, and an entry that no longer matches any violation, both FAIL the\ngate rather than being reported and ignored.\nThe CI gate reads these identities from a live pg_proc built from the real migration\nledger, so nothing here is matched against migration text.\nRemove an entry as soon as the routine it names is hardened.",
